        "original_id": "a55d7fd4-ead2-5d8d-b9b7-35da77ef9f4a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Operation Phantom Linebacker\n- Organizations: 2nd Infantry Division (United States), United States Army, Iraqi National Guard, Iraqi Border Police, Multinational Forces, United States Forces Korea\n- Roles: U.S. 3rd Brigade\n- Places: Iraq, Syria, South Korea\n\nFacts:\n- Operation Phantom Linebacker was a coalition military operation in Iraq designed to interdict anti-government fighters entering Iraq from Syria.\n- The U.S. 3rd Brigade and the 2nd Infantry Division conducted Operation Phantom Linebacker with the Iraqi National Guard, Iraqi Border Police, and other Multinational Forces.\n- The 2nd Infantry Division, also called Indianhead, 2ID, 2nd ID, or Second D, is a formation of the United States Army.\n- The 2nd Infantry Division has about 17,000 soldiers, including 10,000 stationed in South Korea, which is about 35% of United States Forces Korea personnel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "13da8981-1caa-5498-89b0-a68d63ebb6bc",
        "text": "Page: Operation Phantom Linebacker. Sentence: Operation Phantom Linebacker was a coalition military operation in Iraq designed to interdict anti-government fighters from entering Iraq from Syria.\nPage: Operation Phantom Linebacker. Sentence: The U.S. 3rd Brigade and the 2nd Infantry Division (United States) conducted the operation with the Iraqi National Guard, Iraqi Border Police, and other Multinational Forces.\nPage: 2nd Infantry Division (United States). Sentence: The 2nd Infantry Division (\"Indianhead\"; \"2ID,\" \"2nd ID\", or \"Second D\") is a formation of the United States Army.\nPage: 2nd Infantry Division (United States). Sentence: There are approximately 17,000 soldiers in the 2nd Infantry Division, with 10,000 of them stationed in South Korea, accounting for about 35% of the United States Forces Korea personnel.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
